1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,131
In most of America, your tip isn't a

2
00:00:02,141 --> 00:00:02,654
bonus.

3
00:00:02,664 --> 00:00:04,151
Legally, it's part of your server's

4
00:00:04,161 --> 00:00:04,845
wage.

5
00:00:05,020 --> 00:00:06,624
The federal minimum wage for servers

6
00:00:06,634 --> 00:00:08,133
is two dollars and thirteen cents an

7
00:00:08,143 --> 00:00:08,458
hour.

8
00:00:08,468 --> 00:00:10,325
It hasn't changed since 1991.

9
00:00:10,493 --> 00:00:12,027
Restaurants can count your tips toward

10
00:00:12,037 --> 00:00:12,550
the rest.

11
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:14,175
If tips fall short, the owner has to

12
00:00:14,185 --> 00:00:15,426
make up the difference.

13
00:00:15,601 --> 00:00:17,051
So how did it get like this?

14
00:00:17,208 --> 00:00:19,021
After the Civil War, the Pullman Company

15
00:00:19,031 --> 00:00:21,064
hired thousands of Black men, many formerly

16
00:00:21,074 --> 00:00:22,562
enslaved, as porters on its sleeper

17
00:00:22,572 --> 00:00:23,117
trains.

18
00:00:23,232 --> 00:00:24,952
It paid them so little that tips made

19
00:00:24,962 --> 00:00:26,308
up most of their income.

20
00:00:26,459 --> 00:00:27,263
People hated it.

21
00:00:27,273 --> 00:00:29,385
Six states actually made tipping illegal.

22
00:00:29,545 --> 00:00:31,776
Every ban was gone by the late 1920s.

23
00:00:31,786 --> 00:00:33,622
Now, seventy-two percent of Americans

24
00:00:33,632 --> 00:00:35,433
say tipping is expected in more places

25
00:00:35,443 --> 00:00:36,754
than five years ago.

26
00:00:36,975 --> 00:00:37,940
But here's the twist.

27
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:39,821
When Massachusetts voters got the chance

28
00:00:39,831 --> 00:00:41,830
to end the lower tipped wage, they voted

29
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:42,143
no.

30
00:00:42,153 --> 00:00:43,534
By almost two to one.

31
00:00:43,752 --> 00:00:45,147
So should tipping be banned?

32
00:00:45,157 --> 00:00:47,086
Or is it the only way servers make real

33
00:00:47,096 --> 00:00:47,700
money?

